meta {
  name: legacy
  seq: 2
}

auth {
  mode: none
}

docs {
  Routes that exist for compatibility or because a library reverses their URL
  name. **Nothing here is the preferred way to do anything** -- each request says
  what to use instead.

  They are documented rather than deleted because removing a URL name that
  allauth or dj-rest-auth reverses breaks the flow that reverses it. That is
  exactly how the confirmation email broke once: dropping the
  `account_confirm_email` route made `send_email_confirmation()` raise, and no
  signup email went out at all.
}
